# Build context for the API image (backend/Dockerfile).
#
# The image only needs `app/` and `scripts/`, so everything else is excluded
# both to keep the context small and to keep things out of the layer cache.

# Virtualenv — hundreds of MB, and platform-specific: the image installs its
# own Linux wheels from requirements.txt.
.venv/
venv/

# Python bytecode and caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Secrets. Excluded deliberately: the image is environment-driven and must never
# carry credentials, and a `.env` copied into a layer would survive in the image
# even if a later layer deleted it.
.env
.env.*

# Tests are not part of the runtime image. Run them on the host against the venv.
tests/

# PocketBase is a separate image with its own context. This directory holds the
# ~40 MB server binary and, on a working install, `pb_data/` — the live database.
# Copying that into an image would bake the operator's own data (hashed API keys,
# the encrypted Meta token) into a layer, so it is excluded twice over, here and
# in .gitignore.
pocketbase/

# Docs and local tooling state
*.md
.claude/
